Subject: Cantor Identity Admission Judgment Gate P4

@ [specification_uuid] 3c30b3e8-7cd6-4217-aa3e-ab72bd48e0a7
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] d3ae204c-a630-41c4-b532-99a7747d4034

& [Purpose]
  + convert one already rendered accountable-object proposal into a deterministic successor IdentityLedger only when one exact seven-faculty semantic-transition record unanimously clears admission
  + keep inference proposal, constitutional Judgment, objective identity membership, persistent history, and external effect as distinct layers

& [Requirements]
  + [IAG-01] define one deny-unknown-fields AccountableObjectAdmission carrying profile admission identity exact ledger digest candidate object evidence references FacultyCycle and admission digest
  + [IAG-02] validate the current ledger first and refuse a stale expected ledger digest without mutation
  + [IAG-03] require a fully digest-valid candidate at version one whose exact handle is absent from the current basket
  + [IAG-04] require a nonempty admission evidence set equal to the candidate provenance references
  + [IAG-05] validate the complete FacultyCycle through the existing constitutional validator rather than duplicating its ordering boundary projection return or omission logic
  + [IAG-06] require FacultyCycleKind semantic_transition, all seven faculties active, and no omission
  + [IAG-07] bind cycle subject to the candidate handle, before state to a canonical ledger-digest state reference, and after state to the candidate handle
  + [IAG-08] require ObserverDisposition admit
  + [IAG-09] require every activation return accepted with no objection and no uncertainty for this strict first-admission gate
  + [IAG-10] require no unresolved cycle residual
  + [IAG-11] compute and validate an admission digest over every field except itself and reject substitution or tamper
  + [IAG-12] insert exactly one candidate, increment ledger generation exactly once without overflow, recompute digest, and validate the successor
  + [IAG-13] leave the source ledger and proposal unchanged and return no partial successor on every refusal
  + [IAG-14] make equal validated inputs produce byte-equal successor ledgers without clocks randomness IO or hidden state
  + [IAG-15] test success stale base duplicate identity bad version evidence mismatch invalid cycle non-admit qualified return unresolved material binding tamper and deterministic replay
  + [IAG-16] invoke no model infer no external truth persist no journal event expose no MCP operation authorize no effect and publish nothing

& [Delineation]
  + [inside] is exact proposal integrity existing faculty constitutional validation strict unanimous disposition and deterministic in-memory ledger insertion
  + [boundary] is callers construct the candidate evidence and faculty cycle; later work may record an admitted successor in P1 history
  + [outside] is model execution faculty prose generation external truth proof journal mutation MCP persistence authentication effect authority and publication

& [Interpretation]
  + Judgment here is a validated decision record over supplied deliberation, not a claim that deterministic code independently understands the world
